  "narrative": "These new results are conditional persistence tests, not yet formal effect-modification tests. All reported estimates are signed in the registered claim direction; more negative raw outcome means stronger dependency, so a positive signed estimate for a negative-claim contrast still represents stronger dependency.\n\nThe feature_002/feature_010/feature_037 independence panel is decisive. Within feature_002=0, feature_010=1 vs 0 has signed +0.3667 [0.2655, 0.4678] (H71/R59); within feature_002=1, it has +0.5764 [0.4141, 0.7386] (H72/R60). Both intervals lie entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed less-negative direction. I accept these conditional feature_010 claims. This supports the interpretation that the feature_010 association is not simply an artifact of overlap with feature_002.\n\nThe analogous feature_037 persistence tests are also decisive. Within feature_002=0, feature_037=1 vs 0 has signed stronger-dependency estimate +0.8321 [0.7712, 0.8930] (H73/R61); within feature_002=1, it is +0.8088 [0.6781, 0.9395] (H74/R62). I accept both. Reciprocally, feature_002=1 vs 0 persists within feature_037=0 (+0.8217 [0.7612, 0.8822], H77/R63) and within feature_037=1 (+0.8450 [0.7141, 0.9758], H78/R64). These are threshold-level associations within this dataset and strongly suggest that the large feature_002 signal is not eliminated by conditioning on feature_037, nor vice versa. Differences such as feature_010 appearing larger when feature_002=1 than when feature_002=0 are descriptive only; no interaction was requested here, so I do not claim effect modification.\n\nFor feature_063, the pattern supports persistence but is less uniform. H80/R54 gives feature_063=1 vs 0 within feature_002=1 a signed stronger-dependency effect +0.3779 [0.1935, 0.5624], clearly threshold-level; H81/R55 gives +0.2586 [0.1686, 0.3486] within feature_010=0, also threshold-level. I accept H80 and H81. These two results are important because they show that the replicated feature_063 association is not entirely explained away by conditioning on either feature_002 or feature_010.\n\nH79/R53, feature_063 within feature_002=0, gives +0.2325 [0.1327, 0.3323]. The point estimate exceeds threshold and the direction is consistent, but the lower bound is below threshold; because this is a single conditional estimate without independent validation, I keep it unresolved but closed, since H80 already demonstrates feature_063 persistence in the feature_002=1 stratum. H83/R57, feature_063 within feature_037=0, is similarly borderline at +0.2383 [0.1396, 0.3371]. It is scientifically useful to know whether the feature_063 association survives in the feature_037=0 stratum, because the feature_037 main effect is large and in the same stronger-dependency direction. I therefore request one independent validation for H83. H84/R58, feature_063 within feature_037=1, is +0.1316 [-0.0597, 0.3230] with only 58 exposed observations; it is below threshold and imprecise, so it is unresolved but active pending interpretation alongside H83 and the newly registered feature_037 interaction. H82/R56, feature_063 within feature_010=1, is +0.1020 [-0.1869, 0.3909] with 54 exposed observations; it is unresolved and active because the interval is too wide to support or rule out a threshold effect, and the registered feature_010 interaction can test whether attenuation in this stratum is formal effect modification rather than sparse-cell variability.\n\nI registered two exploratory interaction proposals for feature_063 in the feature_010=1 and feature_037=1 strata versus their complements. These are refinements motivated by the conditional differences, not claims of effect modification. Their purpose is to determine whether the apparent attenuation of feature_063 in feature_010=1 or feature_037=1 is supported when the comparison is taken directly against the same-population complement, rather than by comparing two separately conditioned subgroup means.\n\nOverall, the evidence now supports feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 as mutually persistent threshold-level measured associations in the supplied dataset. Feature_063 remains supported overall and persists in at least the feature_002=1 and feature_010=0 strata; its independence from feature_037 is the main remaining conditional question. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or biological mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported threshold-level within-dataset associations: feature_002=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.8315 [0.7658,0.8972] and robustness strata; feature_010=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.4232 [0.3268,0.5195]; feature_037=1 vs 0 stronger-dependency signed +0.8325 [0.7667,0.8983]; feature_063=1 vs 0 stronger-dependency discovery +0.2268 and validation +0.2897. New conditional accepted: feature_010 within feature_002=0 +0.3667 [0.2655,0.4678] (H71) and within feature_002=1 +0.5764 [0.4141,0.7386] (H72); feature_037 within feature_002=0 +0.8321 [0.7712,0.8930] (H73) and within feature_002=1 +0.8088 [0.6781,0.9395] (H74); feature_002 within feature_037=0 +0.8217 [0.7612,0.8822] (H77) and within feature_037=1 +0.8450 [0.7141,0.9758] (H78). This strongly supports mutual persistence among feature_002/010/037 but not formal effect modification. Feature_063 conditional accepted: within feature_002=1 +0.3779 [0.1935,0.5624] (H80) and within feature_010=0 +0.2586 [0.1686,0.3486] (H81). Feature_063 conditional unresolved: H79 f002=0 +0.2325 [0.1327,0.3323] closed; H83 f037=0 +0.2383 [0.1396,0.3371] active pending validation; H82 f010=1 +0.1020 [-0.1869,0.3909] active; H84 f037=1 +0.1316 [-0.0597,0.3230] active. One new validation requested for H83, so voluntary validation budget is now 6. Registered exploratory interactions: feature_063 interaction with f010=1 versus complement (direction positive for attenuation) and feature_063 interaction with f037=1 versus complement. Do not accept effect modification from conditional point differences alone. Next: synthesize H83 validation; if H83 validates, interpret feature_063 as not explained by f037 in f037=0; interactions can be run later only if capacity is useful. Deferred H67-H70 f010/f037 reciprocal pairs and H75-H76 f002 within f010 remain available. Broad untested panels remain: high-prevalence binary indicators, rare binary markers, and categorical levels feature_034/046/054/059/062. Treat all findings as dataset-specific associations, not causal or biological claims.",
