  "narrative": "Current integrated synthesis. The main feature_063 finding is now validated and should be treated as a replicated within-dataset threshold-level association. H44 tested feature_063=1 versus 0 in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. Discovery gave +0.2268 [0.1307, 0.3229], and independent validation gave +0.2897 [0.1426, 0.4369] under the stringent validation interval. Both point estimates exceed the 0.15-unit outcome threshold, the replication is not attenuated, and the intervals exclude zero in the claimed direction. I therefore keep H44 accepted and close the main feature_063 line. The validation lower bound is slightly below threshold, so the exact threshold margin remains uncertain, but the evidence supports a scientifically meaningful association within this dataset.\n\nH91 was the pivotal formal effect-modification test: whether the feature_010 association is enhanced when feature_002=1 relative to its complement. Discovery gave +0.2097 [0.0191, 0.4003], which is above threshold in point estimate but has a lower bound below threshold and close to zero. Independent validation gave +0.1810 [-0.1196, 0.4816], so the validation point remains in the hypothesized direction but does not exclude zero under the stringent interval. The combined evidence is consistent with a small positive interaction but is insufficient to support a threshold-level effect modification claim. I reject H91 as an accepted threshold-level interaction and close that line. This is not proof that feature_010 has no modification by feature_002; it means the evidence does not support the scientifically meaningful interaction claim.\n\nH5 was a response-deadline validation for the main feature_058 marker. Discovery gave +0.0205 [-0.0393, 0.0803] in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, and validation gave +0.0349 [-0.0516, 0.1214]. Both are far below the 0.15 threshold and compatible with no association. I reject H5 and close the main feature_058 line. Combined with earlier feature_007 and feature_015 nulls and the signature-marker interaction nulls, the evidence does not support any of the three research marker assays as main effect predictors in this dataset.\n\nThe supported marker panel is now feature_002, feature_010, feature_037, and feature_063. Within this dataset, feature_002=1 versus 0 is associated with large less-negative composite dependency scores; feature_010=1 versus 0 is associated with less-negative scores; feature_037=1 versus 0 is associated with large stronger-dependency scores; and feature_063=1 versus 0 is associated with stronger-dependency scores, with main-effect validation and conditional persistence evidence. The conditional panel shows that feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 persist under joint clean conditioning, and feature_063 persists in clean and in selected strata, including validated conditioning on feature_037=0. These findings should be interpreted as measured, within-dataset associations and relative persistence of marker associations. They do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.\n\nThe negative and closed lines are also informative. Feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 show no threshold-level main effects, and their main interaction panels with the constructed signatures or each other are not supported. The feature_063 interaction panel by feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 does not support context dependence: H92, H85, and H86 are all below threshold and imprecise, and the sparse subgroup associations H82 and H84 do not revive them. The feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction H91 is now closed as unsupported at the threshold level. Other categorical screens, including feature_054 and many binary/categorical features tested so far, remain null or non-threshold-level.\n\nThe most informative next work is to finish the conditional independence panel and broaden exploration modestly. I have reactivated the reciprocal conditional tests H67-H70 and H75-H76 to complete assessment of feature_010/feature_037 and feature_002/feature_010 dependencies. I also reactivated the rare binary feature_017 test H24 and registered two additional rare binary contrasts, feature_043 and feature_022, in the stronger-dependency direction, plus one categorical contrast for feature_059. I do not plan more feature_063 interactions unless a new conditional estimate emerges with strong motivation. The next analysis should focus on whether these reciprocal conditions support the existing panel or reveal any additional predictor; validation should be reserved for a moderate threshold-level candidate that cannot be resolved from discovery evidence alone.",
  "research_notes": "Updated integrated report after validation response deadlines for H44 and H91 and newly delivered validation for H5.\n\nAccepted threshold-level within-dataset marker panel:\n- feature_002=1 vs 0: large less-negative association; robust in main and multiple conditionals.\n- feature_010=1 vs 0: less-negative association; accepted overall and in key conditionals.\n- feature_037=1 vs 0: large stronger-dependency association; accepted overall and in conditionals.\n- feature_063=1 vs 0: stronger-dependency association; main effect validated (+0.2268 discovery, +0.2897 validation) and persists in clean joint conditionals and several strata, including validated feature_037=0 conditional.\n\nKey conditional persistence evidence:\n- H87 feature_063 among f002=0/f010=0/f037=0: +0.2521 [0.1693,0.3350].\n- H88 feature_010 among f002=0/f037=0: +0.4020 [0.3016,0.5023].\n- H89 feature_037 among f002=0/f010=0: +0.8140 [0.7684,0.8596].\n- H90 feature_002 among f010=0/f037=0: +0.7843 [0.7360,0.8327].\nThese support mutual persistence/relative independence among the four accepted markers within this dataset, not effect modification.\n\nClosed/negative conclusions:\n- H91 feature_010-by-feature_002 interaction rejected: discovery +0.2097 [0.0191,0.4003], validation +0.1810 [-0.1196,0.4816]. No threshold-level effect modification supported.\n- Feature_063 interactions H92, H85, H86 rejected; sparse H82/H84 rejected. Feature_063 remains robust main/conditional marker, not currently context-dependent by f002/f010/f037.\n- H5 feature_058 main effect rejected; discovery +0.0205 [-0.0393,0.0803], validation +0.0349 [-0.0516,0.1214].\n- Research markers f007/f058/f015 main effects and their main interaction panels are not supported.\n- feature_054 line closed null; many tested binary/categorical predictors are subthreshold or inconsistent.\n\nCurrent active next-analysis priorities:\n- Reactivated reciprocal conditionals H67-H70 and H75-H76 to complete independence checks among f010/f037/f002/f010.\n- Reactivated H24 rare binary feature_017.\n- Registered new broad exploratory proposals: feature_043 and feature_022 in stronger-dependency direction, and feature_059 level_001 vs level_003 as an uncertain categorical contrast.\n- Avoid further feature_063 interaction fishing unless a new conditional difference is strong and mechanistically motivated.\n\nValidation status: already validated claims include H5, H39, H40, H44, H59, H83, H91. Five new voluntary validation requests remain. Reserve future validation for a new moderate threshold-level association that needs independent resolution; accepted main/conditional panel signals do not require additional validation at present.\n\nInterpretation discipline: all conclusions are dataset-specific measured associations. No causal inference, biological pathway, therapeutic claim, or external generalizability is asserted. More negative outcome_001 means stronger dependency; accepted positive/negative signed claims follow ledger directions."
