e comparison (H245/R240), and -0.042 [-0.468, 0.385] with feature_063=1 (H249/R244). The reversed interaction persists when feature_063=0 individuals are isolated (+0.817 [0.636, 0.997], H241/R237), and the opposite claimed interaction is rejected (H231/R228). Therefore H238 should be interpreted as loss of the positive feature_010 association at high feature_038, not as evidence that feature_010=1 causes stronger dependency in high-feature_038 individuals. The broader main-effect landscape includes several accepted associations: feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency (+0.832 [0.766, 0.897], H47/R23); feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency (+0.423 [0.327, 0.520], H25/R40) but is strongly modified by feature_038; feature_037=1 is associated with stronger dependency (+0.833 [0.767, 0.898], H30/R42) and this persists within feature_027=1 (+0.658 [0.445, 0.871] discovery; +0.591 [0.143, 1.040] validation, H148/R143/R145); feature_027=1 is associated with stronger dependency (+0.792 [0.676, 0.907], H115/R122; validated +0.826 [0.635, 1.017], R128) and this persists in a clean anchor (+0.754 [0.683, 0.825]; validated +0.799 [0.695, 0.903], H138/R132/R138). Negative findings are numerous. The constructed binary assays feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 show no meaningful threshold-supported main effects or subgroup interactions (for example H4/R4, H5/R5/R76, H6/R6, H10-R21, H13-R18, H46/R172). feature_053 contrasts are broadly null (H33/R18, H34/R18, H175/R177, H176/R177). feature_003 has several point estimates above 0.15 but no robust threshold-supported association after validation or stringent anchoring (H39/R21/R25, H59/R36/R38, H61/R48, H122/R97/R101). feature_031 is not robust: H23/R17 is below threshold and unresolved, while subgroup and validated contrasts reject meaningful negative effects (H62/R31/R102, H63/R32). Many categorical contrasts and interactions involving feature_024, feature_046, feature_052, feature_054, feature_059, feature_061, feature_062, and feature_034 are rejected or remain sparse-cell unresolved. Unresolved uncertainty includes borderline or underpowered heterogeneity: H236 lower bound +0.143, H247 lower bound +0.073 with exposed n=23, H214 interaction lower bound -0.043, H58 interaction lower bound +0.018, and several insufficient-cell comparisons (H1/R1, H2/R2, H3/R3, H9/R9, H125/R100, H173-R176/R176, H194-R199/R222). Sparse invalidity is not evidence of absence. Active unresolved H251 is the most informative next analysis: it tests whether the high-feature_038 feature_063 association persists within feature_037=0, complementing the accepted feature_037=1 and clean-anchor results. If accepted, it would strengthen the claim that feature_063-by-feature_038 heterogeneity is broad across strong predictor strata; if unresolved or rejected, it would delimit the conditional association more narrowly. All conclusions are associations among measured predictors in the supplied dataset only. The endpoint is a composite dependency score, predictor labels are opaque or constructed assays, and multiple testing and exhausted validation mean these results do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability.",
