  "narrative": "No assessments are due, and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so this final exploration registers targeted robustness and decomposition follow-ups rather than new broad screens. The goal is to test whether the accepted conditional associations are carried by correlated large-effect predictors or remain in populations where those predictors are held absent. All new estimates will be already signed to the registered direction, and I will interpret support primarily through the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit absolute threshold, favoring comparisons whose lower bound exceeds that threshold. More negative outcome_001 values denote stronger dependency, so for feature_063, feature_027, and feature_037 comparisons where exposed=1 is expected to have stronger dependency, I use claim direction -1; threshold support appears as a positive signed estimate. For feature_010 attenuation by feature_038, the raw interaction is expected to be negative because the feature_010=1 versus 0 weak-dependency contrast is strong at low feature_038 and near null at high feature_038; using direction -1 therefore yields a positive signed estimate if attenuation is supported. The feature_018 panel is the main unresolved part of the central pattern. The clean-anchor low-feature_018 interaction and the feature_018<=0 high-feature_038 simple contrast under feature_002 absence test whether the strong high-feature_038 feature_063 association persists when feature_018 is low. The feature_018>=0 contrasts under feature_002 or feature_010 absence test whether the currently borderline broad feature_018>=0 high-feature_038 effect becomes stable when one large correlated predictor is absent. If high-feature_038 feature_063 effects are threshold-supported for both feature_018 signs, the best conclusion is that feature_018 is not a decisive modifier; if support remains mainly or only with feature_018<=0, high feature_018 attenuates or delimits the association; sparse or borderline results remain unresolved, not evidence of absence. The feature_010 panel tests whether the accepted feature_038 attenuation persists when feature_002 is absent and when both feature_002 and feature_037 are absent. This distinguishes attenuation that is intrinsic to feature_010/feature_038 from attenuation carried by feature_002 or feature_037. The feature_063/feature_027 panel tests whether the high-feature_038 feature_063 association remains robust when feature_027 is absent, including in populations also lacking feature_037; failure would implicate feature_027 and/or feature_037 as carriers of the signal. The feature_027 panel tests whether the strong high-feature_038 feature_027 association is robust in feature_037 absence, helping to separate correlated strong-dependency predictors. Alternative outcomes are scientifically informative: rejected anchor-specific tests would narrow the accepted conclusions to populations involving the retained predictors, while accepted anchor-specific tests strengthen the dataset-specific conditional patterns without implying causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability."
